<!-- WHY PROJECT MANAGERS CHOOSE VNG -->
<section class="cx-why cx-section" id="why-vng">
  <div class="cx-container">
    <div class="r">
      <div class="cx-eyebrow">Why Project Managers Choose VNG</div>
      <h2 class="cx-h2">The reasons repeat themselves<br>across a thousand projects.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-why-grid stagger">
      <div class="cx-why-item r">
        <div class="cx-why-num">01</div>
        <h3>Deadline Protection</h3>
        <p>When a project falls behind, VNG does not accept the slip — we re-sequence, scale up, and push to recover. Extended hours, weekend crews, whatever the timeline demands. Your handoff date is a commitment, not a target.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-why-item r">
        <div class="cx-why-num">02</div>
        <h3>Itemized Transparency</h3>
        <p>Our quotes list every scope item, every exclusion, every long-lead item and its required order date. No allowances buried in line items. No "unforeseen conditions" that we could have flagged at quote time. What you see is what you pay.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-why-item r">
        <div class="cx-why-num">03</div>
        <h3>One Point of Contact</h3>
        <p>You get a single PM who owns the whole project — every trade, every inspection, every issue. No "talk to my sub" runaround. When something needs to be fixed, the person you call is the person with the authority to fix it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-why-item r">
        <div class="cx-why-num">04</div>
        <h3>Industry-Specific Experience</h3>
        <p>Medical, restaurant, retail, office, industrial — each sector has requirements that trip up generalist contractors. VNG has completed projects across all of them. That experience is not theoretical: it is the reason inspections pass first time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-why-item r">
        <div class="cx-why-num">05</div>
        <h3>Communication You Can Set Your Watch To</h3>
        <p>Structured weekly updates. Immediate escalation on material issues. You never need to chase us for a site report. The people you are managing upward deserve accurate information — we make sure you have it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cx-why-item r">
        <div class="cx-why-num">06</div>
        <h3>Punch Lists That Close</h3>
        <p>We do a full walkthrough before we present you with a punch list. On a typical project, 80% of items close same-day. We do not hand back a job with 60 outstanding items and a crew that has moved on to the next site.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

